likely to be accurately assessed could apply to both the precision of the tool and the validity of the scenario itself. However, if the tools cannot even begin to function because the relationship between the climate driver and the asset is logically flawed, the assessment is not just imprecise; it is fundamentally broken. The most robust direction for the solution is to identify the scenario where the core premise—the intersection of the climate variable and the asset location—is fundamentally misaligned, rendering the entire exercise logically unsound regardless of the tool's technical capacity.\n**Final Answer**"
