tion B was an unverified causal link. Option C was a direct contradiction of the text's description of the scale of the changes. Option D is the only one that relies entirely on the explicit statements found within the text without adding external assumptions. The strongest direction is to identify the specific causal relationship explicitly stated by the company within the text, as this avoids the logical errors of overgeneralization and unsupported causality found in the other options.\n**Final Answer**"
